ollowing surface:\n\n$$\n4{y}^{2}-3{z}^{2}=1,\\,-\\infty <x<\\infty .\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284509 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8f6408ec-2d9a-573b-91f2-4270763372c3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284509 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that the equation of a hyperbolic cylinder whose axis of symmetry is the $z$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nThus, a hyperbolic cylinder whose axis of symmetry is the $x$**-axis** is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{{c}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our equation is a hyperbolic cylinder whose axis of symmetry is the $x$-axis and $b=\\frac{1}{2},\\,c=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284510 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186283943 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284510 #edb/ref 1069 "q-164548" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284510 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284510 #edb/ref 1071 "Identify the following surface:\n\n$$\n{z}^{2}=-12y,\\,-\\infty <x<\\infty .\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284510 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fe349944-268d-5340-92ca-d28764061da5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284510 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that the equation of a parabolic cylinder whose axis is the $z$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}=4py.\n$$\n\nThus, a parabolic cylinder whose axis is the $x$**-axis** is given by\n\n$$\n{z}^{2}=4py.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our equation is a parabolic cylinder whose axis is the $x$-axis and $p=-3.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284511 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186284382 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284511 #edb/ref 1069 "q-164549" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284511 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284511 #edb/ref 1071 "Identify the surface ${y}^{2}-{z}^{2}-x-4y-6z-4=0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284511 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1b66372b-0da7-5bff-8ad5-ecdf16f5fac5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284511 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we complete the square in the $y$ and $z$ terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}-x-4y-6z-4 & =0 \\\\ ({y}^{2}-4y)-({z}^{2}+6z)-x-4 & =0 \\\\ (y-2)^{2}-4-(z+3)^{2}+9-x-4 & =0 \\\\ (y-2)^{2}-(z+3)^{2}+1-x & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, by rearranging, we get the equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-2)^{2}-(z+3)^{2}+1-x & =0 \\\\ (y-2)^{2}-(z+3)^{2} & =x-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the equation of a hyperbolic paraboloid centered at $(1,2,-3).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284512 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186284353 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284512 #edb/ref 1069 "q-164550" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284512 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284512 #edb/ref 1071 "Identify the surface ${x}^{2}-{y}^{2}+2{z}^{2}-2y-8z-9=0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284512 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2297e678-9e2f-50f7-bf32-a9e17f605ed6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284512 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we complete the square in the $y$ and $z$ terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}+2{z}^{2}-2y-8z-9 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-({y}^{2}+2y)+2({z}^{2}-4z)-9 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-(y+1)^{2}+1+2[(z-2)^{2}-4]-9 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-(y+1)^{2}+1+2(z-2)^{2}-8-9 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-(y+1)^{2}+2(z-2)^{2}-16 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, by rearranging, we get the equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-(y+1)^{2}+2(z-2)^{2}-16 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-(y+1)^{2}+2(z-2)^{2} & =16 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}-\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{(z-2)^{2}}{8} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the equation of a hyperboloid of one sheet centered at $(0,-1,2).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321212 #edb/ref 1080 "A hyperboloid of one sheet centered at $(1,1,0)$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321212 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321212 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "085048d0-926b-5cca-8dfa-e564cb57a41d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321601 #edb/ref 1080 "A hyperbolic paraboloid centered at $(0,-2,1)$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [175