] [17592186323754 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186323285 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323754 #edb/ref 1069 "q-36110" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323754 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323754 #edb/ref 1071 "Identify the surface $4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-25{z}^{2}+16x+50z+91=0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323754 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e8b7d35e-9f56-5494-bc85-89ac721410ae" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323754 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we complete the square in the $x$ and $z$ terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-25{z}^{2}+16x+50z+91 & =0 \\\\ 4({x}^{2}+4x)+{y}^{2}-25({z}^{2}-2z)+91 & =0 \\\\ 4[(x+2)^{2}-4]+{y}^{2}-25[(z-1)^{2}-1]+91 & =0 \\\\ 4(x+2)^{2}-16+{y}^{2}-25(z-1)^{2}+25+91 & =0 \\\\ 4(x+2)^{2}+{y}^{2}-25(z-1)^{2}+100 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, by rearranging, we get the equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(x+2)^{2}+{y}^{2}-25(z-1)^{2}+100 & =0 \\\\ 4(x+2)^{2}+{y}^{2}-25(z-1)^{2} & =-100 \\\\ \\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{25}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{100}-\\frac{(z-1)^{2}}{4} & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the equation of a hyperboloid of two sheets centered at $(-2,0,1).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381349 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186381350 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381349 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186381351 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381349 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186381352 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381349 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186381353 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381349 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186381354 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381349 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381349 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381349 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186381350 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381349 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e941d950-316e-5e7e-8eb1-513344452c65" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381350 #edb/ref 1080 "A hyperboloid of one sheet centered at $(-1,0,1)$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186